;; fib.gpu: fibber on a GPU (docs/design/gpu.md). CORE, with no extern (ADR 0011: it emits forms, a driver has the externs): the kernel side is the
;; core form `defkernel` (spec/syntax.md 3.22) and the builtins `gpu/local-id`, `gpu/group-id`, `gpu/group-size`, `gpu/num-groups`,
;; `gpu/global-id`, `gpu/barrier`, `gpu/shared` (spec/types.md 2.17); this facade is the host side: `host-launch` (a kernel run on the CPU over a
;; grid: the one-language guard), the element accessors a kernel uses (`f32-at`, `f32-set!`, ..), the `Device` family of protocols a driver
;; implements (fib.gpu.device: Platform Device Module Kernel Buffer Stream Event Pinned Transfer; errors are values, `GpuError`), the launch ABI (the
;; `fib.kernel-sig` header of a PTX, `parse-signatures`, `check-args`), and the contract any driver must pass (fib.gpu.contract, with the
;; faults of fib.gpu.fault; pinned memory and async copies, gpu.md 13: fib.gpu.contract-async, the host-memory device fib.gpu.sim, the static loan fib.gpu.lend, each an explicit module).
;; Explicit: `(:require [fib.gpu :as gpu])`. The CUDA driver is fib-gpu-cuda, in its own repository; the WebGPU one fib-gpu-webgpu.
(ns fib.gpu (:export-from fib.gpu.host fib.gpu.device fib.gpu.atomic))
